"""Three opening tokens raise the base model Olmo-3-1025-7B from 224 to 410 right answers of 500 on MATH-500 (44.8 % to 82.0 %).

The page of one finding, served at /finding/opening-cue (view.py serves every tools/finding_<slug>.py) and reached from
its tile on /findings, which ICON draws. The picture is one lit plate. At its top, the start of one real answer of the
base model: with the cue on, the cue's three tokens stand lit in front of it. Below, the 500 MATH-500 problems as one dot
each, right or wrong in the run with the plain prompt or in the run with the cue, and the count on a scale with Base, Base
+ cue and RL as marked levels. The reader switches the cue on and off; the dots that change light up or go dark in place.
A click on a dot shows that problem and the start of both answers in the side column.
Address: /finding/opening-cue#<base|cue>/<panel or p<problem>>. Study: studies/rlneurons (README.md "Definitions",
"Established numbers" and "Day-1 #3"; board result-c36598 and result-60d899). The cue is published (Wang et al., arXiv
2610.06851); what this page adds is the share of the RL gain that the cue covers at T 1.0, and that the gap left to RL
depends on the sampling temperature (board result-bac4fd, result-dadeec, result-44b4df).

    python3 tools/finding_opening_cue.py           checks DATA and PROBLEMS against the artifacts
    python3 tools/finding_opening_cue.py --write   rewrites PROBLEMS from the artifacts
"""
